    "id": "train-4210",
    "question": "For the gala luncheon planning committee, Margaret wants to serve chicken salad sandwiches using mini croissants.  She wants there to be enough food that each person on the committee can have 2 sandwiches each.  Her bakery offers 12 minis croissants for $8.00.  There are 24 people on the committee. How much will she spend on croissants?",
    "gold": "32",
    "answer": "There are 24 people on the committee and she wants 2 sandwiches per person so that's 24*2 = <<24*2=48>>48 sandwiches\nShe can buy the croissants by the dozen and she needs 48 croissants so she needs 48/12 = <<48/12=4>>4 dozen croissants\nA dozen croissants cost $8.00 and she needs 4 dozens so that will costs 8*4 = $<<8*4=32.00>>32.00\n#### 32"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Margaret will spend on croissants, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of chicken salad sandwiches needed.\n2. Determine how many sets of 12 mini croissants are required.\n3. Calculate the total cost based on the number of sets needed.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of chicken salad sandwiches needed.**\n\nEach person on the committee will have 2 sandwiches. There are 24 people on the committee.\n\\[\n2 \\text{ sandwiches/person} \\times 24 \\text{ people} = 48 \\text{ sandwiches}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine how many sets of 12 mini croissants are required.**\n\nEach set of 12 mini croissants makes 12 sandwiches.\n\\[\n\\frac{48 \\text{ sandwiches}}{12 \\text{ sandwiches/set}} = 4 \\text{ sets}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the total cost based on the number of sets needed.**\n\nThe bakery offers 12 mini croissants for $8.00. Since Margaret needs 4 sets of 12 mini croissants, we need to find out how many sets of 12 mini croissants are in 4 sets.\n\\[\n4 \\text{ sets} \\times 12 \\text{ mini croissants/set} = 48 \\text{ mini croissants}\n\\]\nSince 48 mini croissants are needed and the bakery offers 12 mini croissants for $8.00, we need to find out how many sets of 12 mini croissants are in 48 mini croissants.\n\\[\n\\frac{48 \\text{ mini croissants}}{12 \\text{ mini croissants/set}} = 4 \\text{ sets}\n\\]\nSince 4 sets of 12 mini croissants cost $8.00, the total cost for 4 sets is:\n\\[\n4 \\text{ sets} \\times \\$8.00/set = \\$32.00\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total amount Margaret will spend on croissants is \\(\\boxed{32}\\).",
